    "---\n",
    "## 1. 3. Modular Programming"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Brief Explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "In modular programming you separate the code into groups that each handle one topic. One group handles the data, another one handles the calculations, and another one handles what gets printed. They work independently and you connect them at the end. It's like having different departments in a company — each one does its own job."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Code Example\n",
    "\n",
    "Complete the steps:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- DATA module: only stores the student info ---\n",
    "def get_students():\n",
    "    return [\n",
    "        {\"name\": \"Ana\",   \"grades\": [70, 80, 90]},\n",
    "        {\"name\": \"Luis\",  \"grades\": [50, 40, 60]},\n",
    "        {\"name\": \"Maria\", \"grades\": [85, 90, 95]},\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- LOGIC module: only does the math ---\n",
    "def calculate(student):\n",
    "    avg = sum(student[\"grades\"]) / len(student[\"grades\"])\n",
    "    passed = avg >= 70\n",
    "    return {\"name\": student[\"name\"], \"average\": avg, \"passed\": passed}\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- REPORT module: only prints ---\n",
    "def show(result):\n",
    "    status = \"PASS\" if result[\"passed\"] else \"FAIL\"\n",
    "    print(f\"{result['name']}: {result['average']:.1f} --> {status}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- connect everything ---\n",
    "for student in get_students():\n",
    "    result = calculate(student)\n",
    "    show(result)"
   ]
  },
